We are building a Laravel 13 application.
Tech Stack: PHP 8.3+, Livewire 4 (Standard & Volt), Flux UI, Tailwind CSS v4, Pest PHP.

Rules for AI generation:

# PHP & Livewire
- Write modern PHP 8.3+ using typed properties, strict types, and arrow functions where appropriate.
- Use Livewire 4 syntax (e.g., use #[Validate] and #[Computed] attributes).
- Use Livewire Volt (single-file components) for simple UI views, and traditional Livewire Class/View pairs for complex logic like the QuoteBuilder.
- Be efficient with data binding: prefer `wire:model.blur` or `wire:model.change` over `wire:model.live` to minimize server requests unless real-time validation is explicitly needed.

# UI & Frontend
- Strictly use Laravel Flux UI components (e.g., <flux:card>, <flux:input>, <flux:button>, <flux:table>) instead of writing raw HTML/Tailwind form elements.
- Keep the UI design clean, minimal, and modern. Do not add arbitrary custom CSS if a Flux component or standard Tailwind utility can handle it.
- Use Tailwind v4 syntax.

# Testing
- When writing tests, strictly use Pest PHP syntax (e.g., `it()`, `test()`, `expect()`) instead of PHPUnit classes.